# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Avatar 90 fps source, no frame generation, -src 90, b:flip present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit. One benchmark test, no fade at either end. The 3:2 case: the target alternates between a real frame and the midpoint of the next pair, and the midpoint present blends only when it lands inside the bare threshold, passing through the hysteresis-widened gate otherwise.
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Avatar 90 fps source, no frame generation, -src 90, b:flip present, -lock -lag 75 -dejit. One benchmark test, no fade at either end. The 3:2 case: the target alternates between a real frame and the midpoint of the next pair, and the midpoint present blends only when it lands inside the bare threshold, passing through the hysteresis-widened gate otherwise.
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 2
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 28.7
src_hint 90.0
# Replay 29.1% / runs 0 / worst 1 / re-seeds 0 against field 28.7% / runs 0 / worst 2. The
# model runs the same widened passthrough gate the relay does, so it reproduces the 41% of
# midpoint presents that pass rather than blend; a rule that closes the 1.5x gap should move
# this fixture to about 50% synth with the worst run still 1, and that is the change this
# bound is meant to fail on, loudly, so the new number gets blessed on purpose.
max_worst_run 1
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 29.5
min_reseeds 0
arrivals 2729
